{
  "world_id": "wld_ashen_measure",
  "name": "The Ashen Measure",
  "description": "Beyond the last breath lies a country of counting-houses, where the dead wait in orderly queues and clerks argue over columns with the gravity of priests and the patience of stones. Here, a soul's account determines the weight placed on the scales—not its worth, the clerks insist, though few find the distinction comforting. When a junior scribe discovers a mortal entered under the wrong heading, the correction must climb a chain of offices designed to make every error someone else's responsibility. The dead do not return to mortal life; only their accounts move. Wry in its paperwork and solemn in its reckonings, the Ashen Measure turns a small clerical discrepancy into a struggle over who gets to define a life.",
